## Where Measurement Disagrees

1. **A member's `default-features = false` on an inherited dependency is
   honoured.** The
   [edition guide](https://doc.rust-lang.org/edition-guide/rust-2024/cargo-inherited-default-features.html)
   says it is rejected when the workspace entry does not itself set it, and
   quotes a warning reading "`default-features` is ignored for regex". On this
   toolchain it is neither ignored nor rejected: `cargo tree -e features -i
   serde` shows `wtx-tags` (which sets it) resolving serde with no `default` and
   no `std`, while `wtx-instrument-db` (which does not) resolves it with both.
   The house rule still puts `default-features = false` on the workspace entry,
   for a reason the doc does not cover: a member override protects only the
   member that writes it, and union resolution reaches the rest.
2. **No canonical essay on feature bloat exists.** Searches return tool READMEs
   and forum threads. Cite `features.html#feature-combinations` (the exponential
   cost, official) and `#mutually-exclusive-features` (split first, official)
   rather than a blog post.

## Contested Upstream, Settled Here

| question                                                     | ecosystem                                                                                                                           | here                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| ------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `default = ["std"]` or no default                            | serde and rand default to `std`; embedded-hal, heapless, bitflags and zerocopy do not                                               | `default` is always written, and never contains `std`. Nothing is published, so the drive-by-host-user ergonomics that motivate `default = ["std"]` buy nothing, and `std` in a default is the hazard §Features describes |
| `std = ["alloc"]` nested, or independent                     | rand nests; serde_core keeps them independent and pays for it with `any(…)` / `all(…, not(…))` at every site                        | nest when both exist, so no call site needs a compound `cfg`                                                                                                                                                              |
| `#![no_std]` or `#![cfg_attr(not(feature = "std"), no_std)]` | Cargo's own example page documents the unconditional form; serde, bitflags and zerocopy use `cfg_attr` with `test` in the predicate | unconditional, so a std use site is gated deliberately rather than compiling the day something unifies `std` on                                                                                                           |

## Version Floors

`dep:` and weak `dep?/feat` — 1.60. Workspace inheritance — 1.64. `[lints]` —
1.74. Optional `package.version` — 1.75. `resolver = "3"` and MSRV-aware
resolution — 1.84. The workspace pins `rust-version = "1.100"` on a nightly
toolchain, so all of it is available and none of it needs guarding.
